<</nobr>>
ElliePlayz   Live
Category: Just Chatting
Viewers: 0

12:17 PM. Early afternoon. Not the graveyard shift   actual daytime Twitch, where the competition is real and the browse page is crowded and the algorithm has to make harder choices about who to surface. This is a tougher test than midnight. If this works here, it works everywhere.

<<chat "ElliePlayz" "Hiii! Oh my gosh, hi! Welcome to my very first stream ever! I'm Ellie, I'm super new to this, I literally just set everything up like twenty minutes ago. I'm SO nervous, haha. Just hanging out today, maybe games later? Come say hi!">>

The voice comes through the monitoring feed and it's the voice from the test   female, warm, a little shy. But there's something else now, something that wasn't there during testing: a performance layer. The way I said "oh my gosh" instead of "oh my god." The way I pitched the nervous laugh. The "haha" that I placed like punctuation, a verbal emoji, the way I've heard Kira do it a thousand times on her stream. I'm not just using a voice modulator. I'm performing a person.

[[Someone's here!|day_3_6_kira]]

