The numbers climb. Not explosively   this isn't a viral moment, a raid, a clip going viral. It's the slow, organic growth of a channel that the algorithm has decided to test. Twitch's recommendation engine works by sampling: it pushes small channels to a handful of viewers, measures the retention, and if the retention is good, it pushes to more. If those viewers stay, it pushes to more. The waterfall effect and ElliePlayz is being watered.

<<chat "stream_viewer_a1" "new streamer alert! followed ✅">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a2" "this voice omggg so soothing">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a3" "what games do you play ellie?">>

