I load Gunmetal Requiem. Queue into a ranked match. Silver 2   the same rank, the same skill, the same person sitting in the same chair at the same desk. The only difference is the voice coming out of the speakers and the name in the corner of the screen.

Round 1: I peek a corner. Get headshot. Dead in three seconds.

<<chat "stream_viewer_a5" "rip 😂">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a2" "awww it's okay ellie! you'll get them next time">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a6" "that was an unfair angle tbh dont feel bad">>

Three seconds into the first round and the chat is already comforting me. Three seconds of failure and the response is warmth. Encouragement. It's okay. When EliPlays dies in three seconds, DarkSlayer posts "LMAO" and strangers leave. When ElliePlayz dies in three seconds, strangers stay and tell her it's unfair.

Viewers: 28

I play through the match. 4 and 9. Terrible. Below average. The kind of scoreboard that, as Eli, would produce dead silence and maybe a bot spam message. As Ellie:

<<chat "stream_viewer_a7" "she's learning! growth mindset queen">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a8" "4 kills is solid for silver tbh">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a2" "ellie you're doing great sweetie">>

