A donation. The notification sound plays through VoxMorph and my gasp   genuine, surprised   comes out softened, feminized, a small "oh!" that sounds like a girl receiving unexpected kindness.

$5.00 from ChillVibesOnly: "new streamer new me. welcome to twitch ellie 💜"

<<chat "ElliePlayz" "Oh my gosh, ChillVibesOnly, thank you SO much! Five dollars! That's   wow. That's my first donation ever. I'm literally shaking right now.">>

I'm not lying about the shaking. My hands are trembling on the keyboard. Five dollars. In twenty-two minutes. As Eli, the last time I received a $5 donation was   I don't actually remember. I don't think I ever have. The largest single donation EliPlays has ever received is $2.50.

Viewers: 41

The number keeps climbing. The chat keeps scrolling. People are talking to each other now   not just to me, but to each other, forming the micro-community that every successful stream needs, the self-sustaining ecosystem of inside jokes and regulars and repeated emotes that turns a viewer into a participant.

<<chat "stream_viewer_a9" "can we get a face reveal eventually? 👀">>

<<chat "ElliePlayz" "Eventually! I promise! I'm just way too nervous right now. I literally look like a mess, haha.">>

<<chat "stream_viewer_a10" "bet you're adorable">>

