The face reveal. They talk about it like it's a season finale   an event they're building toward, a promise I made that carries the weight of anticipation and they're right to anticipate it, because the eyes-only framing IS building something. It's building desire. The invisible lower face is a blank canvas that every viewer fills with their own projection   they imagine the most beautiful version of what they can't see, because the parts they CAN see (the eyes, the lashes, the hair) set the standard high.

Except the face reveal can't happen. Not like this. The jaw would give it away. The lips. The Adam's apple. The face below the nose is still Eli's face   modified at the eye level but fundamentally, structurally masculine from the nose down. A face reveal would end ElliePlayz in the time it takes for one viewer to type "wait is that a dude."

Unless the face changed more.

The thought arrives uninvited, the way the voice modulator idea arrived, the way the RegenaForm consultation arrived   knocking at a door I didn't know existed, polite and inevitable. Unless the face changed more. Unless the jaw softened. Unless the lips filled. Unless the nose refined. Unless Tier 1 continued where it left off this morning, pushing the face further from Eli and closer to Ellie, until the crop line could drop lower and lower and the webcam could show more and more and eventually   eventually   there would be nothing left to hide.

I push the thought away. Not now. Not tonight. Tonight is numbers.

